{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PRF","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This WebAuthn extension wraps the CTAP2 hmac-secret extension, transforming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"PRF secrets into hmac-secret salts using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SHA-256(\"WebAuthn PRF\\0\" + secret)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Simple Usage (single credential)","anchor":"Simple-Usage-single-credential"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let prf = try await WebAuthn.Extension.PRF(session: session)","let ext = try prf.getAssertion.input(first: userSecret)","let params = CTAP2.GetAssertion.Parameters(..., extensions: [ext])","let response = try await session.getAssertion(parameters: params)","if let secrets = try prf.getAssertion.output(from: response) {","    \/\/ Use derived keys","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Multi-credential Usage (evalByCredential)","anchor":"Multi-credential-Usage-evalByCredential"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let prf = try await WebAuthn.Extension.PRF(","    first: defaultSecret,","    evalByCredential: [credIdA: (secretA, nil), credIdB: (secretB, nil)],","    session: session",")","","\/\/ After credential selection:","let ext = try prf.getAssertion.input(for: selectedCredentialId)","let params = CTAP2.GetAssertion.Parameters(..., extensions: [ext])","let response = try await session.getAssertion(parameters: params)","if let secrets = try prf.getAssertion.output(from: response) {","    \/\/ Use derived keys","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pseudo-random function extension for deriving symmetric secrets bound to a credential.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"PRF","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lets a relying party derive deterministic symmetric secrets from a credential","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"— the same input produces the same output every time the user authenticates with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that credential. It’s the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/www.w3.org\/TR\/webauthn-3\/#prf-extension","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for credential-bound key derivation, built on the CTAP2 "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hmac-secret"},{"text":" extension.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The SDK transforms each PRF input with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SHA-256(\"WebAuthn PRF\\0\" || input)"},{"text":" before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sending it to the authenticator — that domain separation is mandated by the spec.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In a high-level WebAuthn flow, configure "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PRF"},{"type":"text","text":" per ceremony via"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Extension\/RegistrationInputs\/prf","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Extension\/AuthenticationInputs\/prf","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"; outputs come back on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clientExtensionResults"},{"type":"text","text":" of the corresponding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Response"},{"type":"text","text":". Registration enables"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"PRF on a credential, optio